<h1>Instant Comparison</h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command is accessible from</span> <span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>3D Inspection &gt; Instant Comparison</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">.</span></p>
<p class="Description"><b><span class="Command" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:normal;">Instant comparison module is useful when one wants to inspect only particular part of an object. Prior to making instant inspection both surfaces (inspected and model) must be registered (see Registration for details) or proper transformation must be active. You can do so using registration tools, datums, transformation creation tools.</span></b></p>
<p><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:normal;">Call</span> <span class="Command">Instant Comparison</span> and the following dialog will appear:</b></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="../images/image2.jpg" width="401px" height="284px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><b><span lang="EN-GB">Enable</span></b></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-GB">Check this box to turn on the instant</span> <span class="Mode">inspection</span> <span lang="EN-GB">mode. The</span> <span class="Mode">Instant Comparison</span> <span lang="EN-GB">mode is disabled by default.</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><b><span lang="EN-GB">Max distance</span></b></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-GB">No points from the inspected surface that are further apart from the reference surface beyond this value, will be inspected. &#160;Default value is 3mm.</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Optimise scan</b></span> section</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Used for aligning patches in order to avoid the arm noise.</p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-GB">Enable</span>  check this box to turn on this process.</b> This option is disabled by default.</p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-GB">Maximum distance</span>  offset of the patches should not exceed this value. Default value is 5mm.</b></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Align entities</b></span> section</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Used for aligning the whole entity in order to fit better to the reference surface:</p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-GB">Enable</span>  check this box to enable these functions.</b> This option is enabled by default.</p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-GB">Sample 1 in every</span>  how many points to be skipped during the processing. Default value is 1.</b></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-GB">Maximum distance</span>  offset of the entity (entities) should not be more than that value. Default value is 3mm.</b></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Point sampling</b></span> section</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Used for reducing the compare process:</p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Auto Sample</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">- KUBE</span> will determine the optimal number of points to be compared in order to get the maximum comparison speed while keeping the quality.</p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-GB">Use ...% of the points</span>  select this if you want to define manually how many points to be used for the inspected surface. For example you can tell KUBE to use 10% or 25% of all points in the comparison. Leave this value to '100%' and each point will be compared. By default this option is switched on with value 100%.</b></p>
<p class="Note" id="p2"><b style="font-weight:bold;">Note<span lang="EN-GB">:</span> When you finish scanning, the first process that starts is Optimise scan, then Align entities, and after that the comparison begins (according to the sampling that you have chosen).</b></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">After setting the parameters, close the dialog and load the mesh that will be used as a reference for inspection (in most cases this should be a CAD model).</span></p>
<p class="Note" id="p3"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note</b></span><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>:</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">Make sure that colours of the CAD model and scan data are different, so while scanning to be easy to see the newly produced patches (go to Entities pane, right click on the CAD model entity, select</span> <span class="Path">Material &gt; Colour</span><span lang="EN-GB">, and choose your colour). Or you can only change the rendering mode of the CAD model to wireframe (go to Entities pane, right click on the CAD model entity, and select</span> <span class="Path">Rendering &gt; Wireframe</span><span lang="EN-GB">.)</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">Now you can start scanning over the model.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">When you finish scanning and exit the</span> <span class="Mode">scan</span> <span lang="EN-GB">mode, the inspection process will begin automatically, providing feedback for the user.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">If you do not scan over the reference, after exiting</span> <span class="Mode">scan</span> <span lang="EN-GB">mode, youll get the following message "</span><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>No overlapped entities.</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">"</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">If the scanned surface overlaps the reference, after completing calculations, the screen on the example below will appear. It shows the scan (or part of it, if the other part is out of inspection range) with colours representing the distance between original (CAD) and scanned (inspected) surface.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Related topic:</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB"><a href="3D_Comparison.htm">Comparison</a></span></p>

